course: dictionary
lesson: 7322
title: Saying it plainly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plainly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. It has three main meanings. It can mean clearly, so that it is easy to see, hear or understand: «She was plainly upset» means anyone could see she was upset.
explain: It can also mean simply, without decoration. A plainly dressed person wears clothes with no lace, bows or sparkles. It can mean honestly and directly too, like «Put plainly, we are going to be late», which means the honest truth said straight out.
explain: To check which meaning fits, swap in clearly, simply or honestly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Plainly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or is done.
fact: «Plainly» means clearly, so that it is easy to see, hear or understand.
fact: «Plainly» can also mean simply, without decoration, or honestly and directly.
fact: Useful phrases with plainly: plainly visible, plainly dressed, put plainly, quite plainly.
fact: Writers say things plainly so that others understand them: «We read it as an old book and say so plainly.»
exercise: «The baby is quite plainly a pig now.» What does plainly mean here? | Quietly, with no sound | *Clearly, so anyone can see it | Happily | Very slowly
exercise: What does plainly dressed mean? | Covered in sparkles | Wearing a costume | Very late for the party | *Simply, with no decoration
exercise: Mum says, «Tell me plainly what happened.» What does she want? | A made-up story with long words | *An honest, direct answer | A whisper | A song about it
test: What does «say so plainly» mean in this sentence: «We read it as an old book and say so plainly»? | Say it in a song | Say nothing at all | Say it in a whisper | *Say it honestly and directly
test: Which phrase means easy to see? | put plainly | plainly dressed | plainly said with a smile | *plainly visible
exam: Which meaning of plainly fits «She was plainly upset»? | *Clearly, so anyone could see it | Politely and kindly | Quickly and quietly | Simply, with no decoration
